A linear transformation is a function between 2 vectors spaces that preserves the operation of vector addition
and scalar multiplication.

This means if T is linear transformation from vector space V to vector space W, then for any vectors it needs to satisfy  2 important properties.

2 important properties:

Additivity T(u+v)=T(u)+T(v)
Multiplicity T(cu)=cT(u)

u,v belongs to V
c is a scalar value
T:V->W} linear transfomation

